<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1 (Monotonic Policy Improvement). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> Proof</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix state <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{+}=\{a:\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)\geq\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{+}=\{a:\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)\geq\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{-}=\{a:\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)&lt;\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{-}=\{a:\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)&lt;\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> upweights actions with higher rewards, there exists threshold <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(s)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}(s,a)\geq q(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}(s,a)\geq q(s)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}(s,a)\leq q(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}(s,a)\leq q(s)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}_{-}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\pi^{*}_{\lambda}}(s)-V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\pi^{*}_{\lambda}}(s)-V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{+}}(\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)-\pi_{\beta}(a|s))r^{*}(s,a)+\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{-}}(\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)-\pi_{\beta}(a|s))r^{*}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{+}}(\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)-\pi_{\beta}(a|s))r^{*}(s,a)+\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{-}}(\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)-\pi_{\beta}(a|s))r^{*}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq q(s)\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{+}}(\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)-\pi_{\beta}(a|s))+q(s)\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{-}}(\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)-\pi_{\beta}(a|s))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq q(s)\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{+}}(\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)-\pi_{\beta}(a|s))+q(s)\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}_{-}}(\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)-\pi_{\beta}(a|s))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=q(s)\left(\sum_{a}\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)-\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\right)=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=q(s)\left(\sum_{a}\pi^{*}_{\lambda}(a|s)-\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\right)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3 (Policy Improvement Under Noisy Rewards). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> Proof</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1:<span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> First we derive a high probability bound for the error <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>. Since each <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-sub-Gaussian, for any <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and any action <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and state <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{P}(|\xi(s,a)|\geq t)\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{P}(|\xi(s,a)|\geq t)\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying a union bound over all <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{A}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{A}|</annotation></semantics></math> actions:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{P}\left(\exists a\in\mathcal{A}:|\xi(s,a)|\geq t\right)\leq 2|\mathcal{A}|\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{P}\left(\exists a\in\mathcal{A}:|\xi(s,a)|\geq t\right)\leq 2|\mathcal{A}|\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Setting the right-hand side equal to <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and solving for <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2|\mathcal{A}|\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)=\delta\implies t=\sigma\sqrt{2\log(2|\mathcal{A}|/\delta)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2|\mathcal{A}|\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)=\delta\implies t=\sigma\sqrt{2\log(2|\mathcal{A}|/\delta)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon:=\sigma\sqrt{2\log(2|\mathcal{A}|/\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon:=\sigma\sqrt{2\log(2|\mathcal{A}|/\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then with probability at least <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi(s,a)|\leq\epsilon\quad\forall a\in\mathcal{A}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi(s,a)|\leq\epsilon\quad\forall a\in\mathcal{A}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">We condition on this event for the remainder of the proof. Additionally, we fix a state <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and assume <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\beta}(a|s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\beta}(a|s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2:<span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Now we can proceed to compare <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\propto\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(\hat{r}(s,a)/\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\propto\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(\hat{r}(s,a)/\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is the exponential tilt using noisy rewards <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}=r^{*}+\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}=r^{*}+\xi</annotation></semantics></math>. From Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Exponential Reward-Weighted Policy Optimization ‣ 3 Background ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, we know that <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\lambda}(\cdot|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\lambda}(\cdot|s)</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique maximizer of</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F(\pi)=\sum_{a}\pi(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)-\lambda\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\pi(\cdot|s)\|\pi_{\beta}(\cdot|s)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\pi)=\sum_{a}\pi(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)-\lambda\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\pi(\cdot|s)\|\pi_{\beta}(\cdot|s)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">In particular, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\pi_{\lambda})\geq F(\pi_{\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\pi_{\lambda})\geq F(\pi_{\beta})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\beta}\|\pi_{\beta})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\beta}\|\pi_{\beta})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, this gives:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)-\lambda\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi_{\lambda}\|\pi_{\beta})\geq\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)-\lambda\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\pi_{\lambda}\|\pi_{\beta})\geq\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\lambda}\|\pi_{\beta})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\lambda}\|\pi_{\beta})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the left-hand side is at most <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>, so:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)\geq\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)\geq\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to convert this inequality on noisy rewards into an inequality on true rewards. Since <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi(s,a)|\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi(s,a)|\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\lambda}(\cdot|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\lambda}(\cdot|s)</annotation></semantics></math> is a probability distribution:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)=\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,r^{*}(s,a)=\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,(\hat{r}(s,a)-\xi(s,a))\geq\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)-\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)=\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,r^{*}(s,a)=\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,(\hat{r}(s,a)-\xi(s,a))\geq\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)-\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, since <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}(s,a)=r^{*}(s,a)+\xi(s,a)\geq r^{*}(s,a)-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}(s,a)=r^{*}(s,a)+\xi(s,a)\geq r^{*}(s,a)-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)\geq\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\,(r^{*}(s,a)-\epsilon)=V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)-\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)\geq\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\,(r^{*}(s,a)-\epsilon)=V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)-\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Chaining (<a href="#A1.E25" title="Equation 25 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.2 Theorem Proof ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>), (<a href="#A1.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.2 Theorem Proof ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>), and (<a href="#A1.E26" title="Equation 26 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.2 Theorem Proof ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\geq\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)-\epsilon\geq\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)-\epsilon\geq V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)-2\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\geq\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)-\epsilon\geq\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\,\hat{r}(s,a)-\epsilon\geq V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)-2\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\sigma\sqrt{2\log(2|\mathcal{A}|/\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\sigma\sqrt{2\log(2|\mathcal{A}|/\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4.4 (Temperature-Dependent Bound). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> Proof</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under the conditions of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3 (Policy Improvement Under Noisy Rewards). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, if rewards are bounded <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}(s,a)\in[0,R_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}(s,a)\in[0,R_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math>, then with probability at least <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\geq V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)-R_{\max}\left(e^{2\epsilon/\lambda}-1\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\geq V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)-R_{\max}\left(e^{2\epsilon/\lambda}-1\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\sigma\sqrt{2\log(2|\mathcal{A}|/\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\sigma\sqrt{2\log(2|\mathcal{A}|/\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 2\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 2\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, this simplifies to:</p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\geq V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)-\frac{4R_{\max}\epsilon}{\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\geq V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)-\frac{4R_{\max}\epsilon}{\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">As before, let <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)=\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(r^{*}(s,a)/\lambda)/Z^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)=\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(r^{*}(s,a)/\lambda)/Z^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the exponential tilt under true rewards, and <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)=\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(\hat{r}(s,a)/\lambda)/Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)=\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(\hat{r}(s,a)/\lambda)/Z</annotation></semantics></math> the tilt under noisy rewards, where <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{*}=\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(r^{*}(s,a)/\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{*}=\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(r^{*}(s,a)/\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(\hat{r}(s,a)/\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(\hat{r}(s,a)/\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> are the normalizing factors. As in Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3 (Policy Improvement Under Noisy Rewards). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, we condition on the event <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi(s,a)|\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi(s,a)|\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, which holds with probability at least <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and fix the state <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, the value function can be decomposed as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)-V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)=\underbrace{\left(V^{\pi_{\lambda}^{*}}(s)-V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)\right)}_{\geq\,0\text{ by Proposition~\ref{prop:monotonic}}}-\underbrace{\left(V^{\pi_{\lambda}^{*}}(s)-V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\right)}_{\text{noise difference}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext> by Proposition </mtext><mtext><a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1 (Monotonic Policy Improvement). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>noise difference</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)-V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)=\underbrace{\left(V^{\pi_{\lambda}^{*}}(s)-V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)\right)}_{\geq\,0\text{ by Proposition~\ref{prop:monotonic}}}-\underbrace{\left(V^{\pi_{\lambda}^{*}}(s)-V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\right)}_{\text{noise difference}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we just need to bound the difference between the noisy and noise-free policy values. Since <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}(s,a)\in[0,R_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}(s,a)\in[0,R_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|V^{\pi_{\lambda}^{*}}(s)-V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|V^{\pi_{\lambda}^{*}}(s)-V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\sum_{a}\left(\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)-\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\right)r^{*}(s,a)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\sum_{a}\left(\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)-\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\right)r^{*}(s,a)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq R_{\max}\sum_{a}\left|\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)-\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq R_{\max}\sum_{a}\left|\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)-\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=2R_{\max}\,D_{\mathrm{TV}}\!\left(\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(\cdot|s),\,\pi_{\lambda}(\cdot|s)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2R_{\max}\,D_{\mathrm{TV}}\!\left(\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(\cdot|s),\,\pi_{\lambda}(\cdot|s)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the noise weight <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(a)=\exp(\xi(s,a)/\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(a)=\exp(\xi(s,a)/\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi(s,a)|\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi(s,a)|\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="e^{-\epsilon/\lambda}\leq w(a)\leq e^{\epsilon/\lambda}\quad\forall\,a\in\mathcal{A}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-\epsilon/\lambda}\leq w(a)\leq e^{\epsilon/\lambda}\quad\forall\,a\in\mathcal{A}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we relate the noisy and clean policies. Since <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}(s,a)=r^{*}(s,a)+\xi(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}(s,a)=r^{*}(s,a)+\xi(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>, the noisy partition function factorizes as:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp\!\left(\frac{\hat{r}(s,a)}{\lambda}\right)=\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp\!\left(\frac{r^{*}(s,a)}{\lambda}\right)\exp\!\left(\frac{\xi(s,a)}{\lambda}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp\!\left(\frac{\hat{r}(s,a)}{\lambda}\right)=\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp\!\left(\frac{r^{*}(s,a)}{\lambda}\right)\exp\!\left(\frac{\xi(s,a)}{\lambda}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp\!\left(\frac{r^{*}(s,a)}{\lambda}\right)w(a)=Z^{*}\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)\,w(a)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a}\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp\!\left(\frac{r^{*}(s,a)}{\lambda}\right)w(a)=Z^{*}\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)\,w(a),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last step uses <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)=\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(r^{*}(s,a)/\lambda)/Z^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)=\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(r^{*}(s,a)/\lambda)/Z^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Dividing both sides by <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{Z}{Z^{*}}=\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)\,w(a)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{Z}{Z^{*}}=\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)\,w(a),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the partition function ratio is simply the expected noise weight under the clean policy. Combined with (<a href="#A1.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.3 Theorem Proof ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>), this gives <math id="A1.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="e^{-\epsilon/\lambda}\leq Z/Z^{*}\leq e^{\epsilon/\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-\epsilon/\lambda}\leq Z/Z^{*}\leq e^{\epsilon/\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="e^{-\epsilon/\lambda}\leq\rho\leq e^{\epsilon/\lambda},\quad\text{where }\rho:=Z^{*}/Z." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where </mtext><mi>ρ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>Z</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-\epsilon/\lambda}\leq\rho\leq e^{\epsilon/\lambda},\quad\text{where }\rho:=Z^{*}/Z.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any action <math id="A1.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, the policy ratio between the noisy and clean policies then follows directly:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)}{\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)}=\frac{\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(\hat{r}(s,a)/\lambda)/Z}{\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(r^{*}(s,a)/\lambda)/Z^{*}}=w(a)\cdot\frac{Z^{*}}{Z}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\pi_{\lambda}(a|s)}{\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)}=\frac{\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(\hat{r}(s,a)/\lambda)/Z}{\pi_{\beta}(a|s)\exp(r^{*}(s,a)/\lambda)/Z^{*}}=w(a)\cdot\frac{Z^{*}}{Z}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting (<a href="#A1.E35" title="Equation 35 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.3 Theorem Proof ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) into the total variation:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\,D_{\mathrm{TV}}\!\left(\pi_{\lambda}^{*},\,\pi_{\lambda}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\,D_{\mathrm{TV}}\!\left(\pi_{\lambda}^{*},\,\pi_{\lambda}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)\left|w(a)\,\rho-1\right|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>a</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a}\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(a|s)\left|w(a)\,\rho-1\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">From (<a href="#A1.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.3 Theorem Proof ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E34" title="Equation 34 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.3 Theorem Proof ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>), the product <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(a)\,\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(a)\,\rho</annotation></semantics></math> lies in <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[e^{-2\epsilon/\lambda},\,e^{2\epsilon/\lambda}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[e^{-2\epsilon/\lambda},\,e^{2\epsilon/\lambda}]</annotation></semantics></math>, so:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|w(a)\,\rho-1|\leq\max\!\left(e^{2\epsilon/\lambda}-1,\;1-e^{-2\epsilon/\lambda}\right)=e^{2\epsilon/\lambda}-1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|w(a)\,\rho-1|\leq\max\!\left(e^{2\epsilon/\lambda}-1,\;1-e^{-2\epsilon/\lambda}\right)=e^{2\epsilon/\lambda}-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the equality holds because <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{x}-1\geq 1-e^{-x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{x}-1\geq 1-e^{-x}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting back into (<a href="#A1.E36" title="Equation 36 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.3 Theorem Proof ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A1.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{TV}}\!\left(\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(\cdot|s),\,\pi_{\lambda}(\cdot|s)\right)\leq\frac{e^{2\epsilon/\lambda}-1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{TV}}\!\left(\pi_{\lambda}^{*}(\cdot|s),\,\pi_{\lambda}(\cdot|s)\right)\leq\frac{e^{2\epsilon/\lambda}-1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting (<a href="#A1.E38" title="Equation 38 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.3 Theorem Proof ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>) into (<a href="#A1.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.3 Theorem Proof ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) and then into (<a href="#A1.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.3 Theorem Proof ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Robust Post-Training for Generative Recommenders: Why Exponential Reward-Weighted SFT Outperforms RLHF" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A1.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\geq V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)-R_{\max}\!\left(e^{2\epsilon/\lambda}-1\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\geq V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)-R_{\max}\!\left(e^{2\epsilon/\lambda}-1\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 2\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 2\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\epsilon/\lambda\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\epsilon/\lambda\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{x}-1\leq 2x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{x}-1\leq 2x</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, giving:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\geq V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)-\frac{4R_{\max}\,\epsilon}{\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi_{\lambda}}(s)\geq V^{\pi_{\beta}}(s)-\frac{4R_{\max}\,\epsilon}{\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\sigma\sqrt{2\log(2|\mathcal{A}|/\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\sigma\sqrt{2\log(2|\mathcal{A}|/\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experiments</h2>

